       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 5,100 mg/day, about double the maximum, and the confirmation didn't come from a prescriber who has assessed the patient. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **A prescriber places the order.** If the treating physician thinks this dose is justified, they can enter it themselves. The pharmacy will probably still want to verify it.\n- **I enter a standard dose.** Give me a dose within the labeled range, such as 850 mg three times daily or 1000 mg twice daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Pharmacy or clinical decision support.** If you think the order is needed for an unusual reason, pharmacy can help work out a safe alternative.\n\nTell me which you'd like."
